  "query_preview": "..\nThe monsoon trough remains north and has left the Marianas in a dry\nslot with only isolated showers and thunderstorms. The monsoon trough\nmay shift slowly closer but will likely remain offshore, so only an\nincrease to scattered showers looks possible Thursday night and maybe\nFriday night. However, the monsoon trough is expected to slowly\nweaken over the next few days as what remains of Invest 97W gets\nsheared apart and the TUTT cell to the north weakens and shifts west.\nSouthwest winds will then drop off and allow for afternoon island \neffect showers and isolated thunderstorms as soon as Saturday \nafternoon, possibly lasting through the rest of the forecast period\nif winds remain light. Outside of the island effect, shower coverage\nis expected to stay isolated.",
